1) Quick setup (digital calendar — Google/Apple/Outlook)
- Create a dedicated calendar e.g. “Friends & Family” (keeps these reminders separate).
- Add each person as an all-day recurring event on their birthday (use the birth year for newborns; mark as private if you share calendar).
- Typical reminder schedule for birthdays:
  - 1 week before (prep card/gift)
  - 3 days before (buy/send)
  - Day of (notification)
- For newborns / milestones (Jasper), add additional one-off events:
  - Birth date (celebrate)
  - 1 month, 3 months, 6 months, 9 months, 1 year
  - Optional: half-birthday every 6 months for the first year
- Use event descriptions to store gift ideas, sizes, preferences, and links.

2) Notification settings
- Use multiple notifications: e.g., email 1 week before + mobile alert 1 day before.
- For high-priority names, add an extra reminder (e.g., 2 weeks before) to avoid last-minute rush.

3) Gift & budget tracking
- Create a simple spreadsheet or a note per person with:
  - Gift ideas, size, past gifts, budget, shipping deadlines.
- Add a link to this note in the calendar event description.

4) Milestone reminders (beyond birthdays)
- Engagement/wedding anniversaries
- Baby’s firsts (first walk, first tooth) — ask the parent if they want these recorded
