5) Physical planner option
- Use a wall calendar or planner and mark birthdays with colored stickers; keep a “gift drawer” with cards and stamps.
- Keep a pocket notebook or your Book Lover’s Journal with short notes/ideas.

6) Sharing & collaboration
- Create a shared family calendar or folder with your partner/aunt/family so others can add/update events.
- For groups of friends, a shared Google Sheet or Slack channel can centralize gift coordination.

7) Automation & tools
- If you use Facebook contacts, enable calendar sync (imports birthdays).
- Use IFTTT / Zapier: e.g., when a new contact with birthday is added to your phone, auto-create a calendar event.
- Apps to consider: Google Calendar (cross-platform), Fantastical (Mac/iOS), Any.do or Todoist (reminder + tasks), Birthday Calendar+ (birthday-focused).

8) CSV import template (if you want to bulk import)
